  "description": "Choi Woo-Sang, who sat diagonally across from me, Choi Woo-Sang who smiled at my outspoken compliments, Choi Woo-Sang who strangely comforted me by saying, \"You're pretty.\"\n\nChoi Woo-Sang who hurt me. \n\nChoi Woo-Sang, whom I met again at a class reunion after more than ten years. He's still unlucky, still hot-headed, and I still hate him. Thinking they'd never meet again, Soo-Han turns away from Woo-Sang, but Woo-Sang, as if his steps had been meaningless, comes to the store where Soo-Han works and starts harassing him.\n\n *\"You've been selling your body, haven't you? Do you think money is everything to you?!\"\n\n\"Yeah, money is everything to me.\"*\n\nWhat kind of misunderstanding is this? How can I get you off my back? \n\n *\"Then it'll be my money too?\"*\n\nWhat bigger change will there be if another layer of lies is spread between us?\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)\n\n*Note: Includes 17 extra chapters.*",
